 # API

-JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.
+JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`; besides those,
+`GET /audit` lists the audit log (see below).
+
+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are stored in the
+data file under `apiKeys` (`key`, `name`, `role`); there is no route to
+manage them. The roles:
+
+- `viewer`: reads only (`GET`), except the audit log.
+- `cook`: as viewer, plus `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures` and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: everything, including `GET /audit`.
+
+A request without a key or with an unknown key answers 401 `unauthorized`
+(before any other check, so unknown routes are 401 too); a known key whose
+role may not use the route answers 403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Audit log
+
+Every request that is not a `GET` and carries a known key, whether it
+succeeded or not, writes an audit entry `{ id, at, keyName, method, path,
+status }` (`path` without the query string). `GET /audit` lists the entries
+newest first, for managers only. Keys themselves never appear in it.

